<description>
Trace a green path from the start, turning right at pink controls and left at teal controls until it exits the grid.

Input structure
- A black-background grid contains exactly one green start pixel.
- The remaining foreground pixels are pink and teal one-pixel turn controls.
- The green start has exactly one cardinal sightline whose first non-background pixel is a turn control.

Rule
- Begin moving from the green start toward that visible control.
- Paint green through background cells in a straight line.
- When the next cell is a pink control, turn right without overwriting it; when it is a teal control, turn left without overwriting it.
- Stop when the next step would leave the grid.

Key insight
- The colored control pixels are not targets to fill; they are turn instructions for a single ray that leaves a continuous green trail.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single green start pixel with pink and teal turn-control pixels",
  "path": "begin along the unique cardinal sightline from the start to a control; travel straight through background cells, turning right immediately before each pink control and left immediately before each teal control, stopping at the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "paint every visited background pixel green",
  "transform": "preserve the original green start and all pink/teal controls"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-10 rows x 6-12 cols, black background
  start:
    color: green, exactly 1 pixel
    position: always on left edge (col=0), row varies [observed]
  controls:
    colors: pink (turn right 90deg) and teal (turn left 90deg), each 1 pixel
    count: 1-6 total, all visited by path (no distractors)
    at_least_one_type: may have 0 of one type but >=1 total
  path:
    initial_direction: rightward (0,+1) from green start toward first control on same row
    segments: 2 to 7 straight segments separated by turns at controls
    segment_length: 1-4 cells each
    total_path_cells: 5-17 (new green cells painted)
    termination: path exits grid edge after last segment
    no_self_crossing: path cells never overlap each other or controls
  output:
    paint all traversed background cells green
    preserve green start and all pink/teal controls unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H x W in [6..10] x [6..12].
    2. Pick number of turns T in [1..6]. Pick turn sequence of R(pink)/L(teal).
    3. Place green start at (random row, col=0). Set direction = rightward.
    4. Build path forward by choosing segment lengths (1-4 cells each).
       After each segment, place the control pixel at the next cell in current
       direction. Apply the turn. Repeat T times.
    5. After last turn, extend final segment so it exits the grid edge.
       If any segment goes out of bounds or overlaps, retry from step 3.
    6. Record all path cells (output has them green) and control positions.
    7. Input = grid with only green start + control pixels; output = input + green path.
```
